    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f50dc151-27df-3689-8ade-3c983a65625d",
                "word": "PTB",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37c00aaf-af6f-3855-a893-ebd9a24f42b1",
                        "entry_id": "f50dc151-27df-3689-8ade-3c983a65625d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Proto-Tibeto-Burman"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b1ba9da-f649-4774-959d-cffe48709078",
                                "sense_id": "37c00aaf-af6f-3855-a893-ebd9a24f42b1",
                                "text": "[E]ven reconstructed syllable-initial units, such as his Proto-Tibeto-Burman (PTB) and PLB [Proto-Lolo-Burmese] prefixed spirantal initial *C-s and his PTB and PLB voiceless spirantal initial *s [...] draw on syllable features and syllable-final features for their reflexes"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32afef95-ce4c-4155-8829-022ba09a0040",
                                "sense_id": "37c00aaf-af6f-3855-a893-ebd9a24f42b1",
                                "text": "The Lahu verb tā ‛place on; put on; set on; stand sthg. upright’ has impeccable Tibeto-Burman credentials⁹, reflecting PLB *ˀta² (cf. WB thâ) and ultimately PTB *s-ta (cf. WT sta ᛝ stad)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b29844b-7d2e-456c-9c8e-e0c83f93f8bf",
                                "sense_id": "37c00aaf-af6f-3855-a893-ebd9a24f42b1",
                                "text": "PTB had six vowels: /i, e, ɑ, o, u, ə/ while only five /i, e, ɑ, o, u/ were present in Classical Tibetan."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                "word": "PTB",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "25b8026a-350d-45cd-9d59-2603f18e09df",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "PTBs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e134090c-c9b1-3ac7-b21f-381a07f5944d",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of powers that be."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism",
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6502fc5-2c74-3fe7-bebc-51c606c28f9a",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of preterm birth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "643259a9-89e8-418b-b3a2-47c832805e0f",
                                "sense_id": "d6502fc5-2c74-3fe7-bebc-51c606c28f9a",
                                "text": "OBJECTIVE: To determine the value of single versus multiple markers of altered vaginal flora to predict subsequent PTB (<37 weeks' gestation, [wks GA]) and the efficacy of treatment with metronidazole plus erythromycin (M+E) to reduce PTB in these patients."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4487bb0e-dde6-4f44-97a6-09819434d095",
                                "sense_id": "d6502fc5-2c74-3fe7-bebc-51c606c28f9a",
                                "text": "Understanding the risks associated with spontaneous PTBs that are unique to African American women and why biopsychosocial risk factors vary by racial/ethnic group may lead to tailored interventions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e696684c-fd9f-49e3-8417-bbd6fe6ce1c9",
                                "sense_id": "d6502fc5-2c74-3fe7-bebc-51c606c28f9a",
                                "text": "Early identification of women at high risk of PTB is important, given the availability of evidence-based, effective screening modalities, which facilitate decision-making on preventative strategies, particularly transvaginal sonographic cervical length (CL) measurement."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f72d6987-4af5-3e25-9812-effcb5117359",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of pulmonary tuberculosis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c11d863-cdf8-4d00-8665-8028ce1b900f",
                                "sense_id": "f72d6987-4af5-3e25-9812-effcb5117359",
                                "text": "Under the circumstances above narrated, we find that claimant's illness of PTB, which flared up or has activated as a result of the nature and condition of his work, is compensable under the law."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5e16cb3-e74a-426c-ae39-1d04869f3c3e",
                                "sense_id": "f72d6987-4af5-3e25-9812-effcb5117359",
                                "text": "Furthermore, a recent study [...] of BCG [Bacille Calmette Guérin vaccine] efficacy in children under 7 years of age who had lived in close contact with undiagnosed cases of PTB showed a protection rate of 70% against the disease within a 6 months follow-up period."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "74bd47d7-dfec-41e5-9129-75ccc7f84025",
                                "sense_id": "f72d6987-4af5-3e25-9812-effcb5117359",
                                "text": "We will perform subgroup analysis and meta-regression analysis based on [...] different types of PTBs[.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7be35410-f4d4-3f07-ba71-1a57fd22f860",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of polypyrimidine tract-binding protein."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "465e7ab0-a9fc-4874-8b3c-edc5b362baac",
                                "sense_id": "7be35410-f4d4-3f07-ba71-1a57fd22f860",
                                "text": "PTB was first purified as a polypeptide that binds to the polypyrimidine tract that typically precedes the 3′ splice sites of higher eukaryotic mRNA introns [1]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7e2e776-3418-44dc-8bc1-9f7cc31af99a",
                                "sense_id": "7be35410-f4d4-3f07-ba71-1a57fd22f860",
                                "text": "Specificity of PTB function is achieved by a combination of changes in the cellular localization of this protein (its ability to shuttle from the nucleus to the cytoplasm is tightly controlled) and its interaction with additional proteins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8cd2470-d315-4f7c-907d-27275dbab2cf",
                                "sense_id": "7be35410-f4d4-3f07-ba71-1a57fd22f860",
                                "text": "These findings suggest that supplementing cholinergic neurons after PTB knockdown may be a promising therapeutic strategy to revert depression-like behaviors and cognitive impairment."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "200172b1-cb82-3fe2-afdf-fc430e5a2c57",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of public test build, public test branch."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "22e7505f-b1ed-4f62-995b-e25b818a5d72",
                                "sense_id": "200172b1-cb82-3fe2-afdf-fc430e5a2c57",
                                "text": "The developer clarified that players will be able to enjoy all of these changes and new Stranger Things content until the end of the PTB[.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54be276f-7aea-4a59-a37f-10831ff8d6dd",
                                "sense_id": "200172b1-cb82-3fe2-afdf-fc430e5a2c57",
                                "text": "The clients targeted for this injection are Discord, Discord Development, Discord Canary, and Discord PTB (Public Test Build)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ca0418c-76d5-4ab1-af9c-94e9c76ded6a",
                                "sense_id": "200172b1-cb82-3fe2-afdf-fc430e5a2c57",
                                "text": "Those who wish to participate need good internet as these PTBs require them to practically reinstall the whole game."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a963530a-6654-48a4-abc4-bb3347a155d5",
                                "sense_id": "200172b1-cb82-3fe2-afdf-fc430e5a2c57",
                                "text": "A new PTB update has arrived for Dead by Daylight, and it offers a whole bunch of new things for players to check out."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eed0474f-3337-4121-a829-912a4313e1d9",
                                "sense_id": "200172b1-cb82-3fe2-afdf-fc430e5a2c57",
                                "text": "It is worth keeping in mind, while you can test the Ashlands biome on the PTB, it’s still in development meaning you may experience more glitches and bugs while playing on the PTB."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eba0a0c8-bb79-340d-9ba0-f040bf86ffc0",
                        "entry_id": "b56aae8f-540d-31b6-b1d8-5c678cab14d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of packet too big, an IPv6 error message."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e36af443-ea37-44b9-ad2e-80f755d0c2d8",
                                "sense_id": "eba0a0c8-bb79-340d-9ba0-f040bf86ffc0",
                                "text": "I'm 90% sure that FreeBSD itself will do this when it receives a PTB with an MTU value of (say) 1000."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e83b9ebe-f560-4563-9e81-e1eccd0327d5",
                                "sense_id": "eba0a0c8-bb79-340d-9ba0-f040bf86ffc0",
                                "text": "Therefore, receiving a PTB message with a ^([sic]) MTU smaller thatn the IPv6 minimum MTU of 1280 bytes causes a host to append a fragmentation header to all its IPv6 packages to a certain host."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1b636a6-8a8d-4cc3-a0b5-1e960a49a3da",
                                "sense_id": "eba0a0c8-bb79-340d-9ba0-f040bf86ffc0",
                                "text": "[F]irewalls that completely block incoming PTBs break the PMTUD protocol."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
